# {{ benchmark_name }} Service

## Getting started

{% if template == "vals-ai" %}This service includes Vals authentication, provider routes, and fixed dataset versions. Follow the [benchmark onboarding guide](https://www.notion.so/vals-ai/Adding-a-New-Benchmark-to-Valkyrie-End-to-End-Guide-36e8a877dd8d816595e6cf35248cb9a6) for the full Valkyrie workflow.

Replace the examples in `dataset/splits/public/`. Each task has `task.toml`, a public question in `instruction.md`, and a private expected answer in `answer.json`. Edit `load_tasks` in `src/{{ benchmark_package }}/benchmark_service.py` if your file format differs. `config/routes.json` maps the API's `default` dataset to this collection's `public` task group.

The service already loads saved datasets. Adapt the execution and grading methods for your benchmark:
{% else %}Edit `src/{{ benchmark_package }}/benchmark_service.py` and implement the six abstract methods on `ExampleBenchmark`:
{% endif %}

| Method | What to do |
|--------|------------|
{% if template == "default" %}| `load_datasets()` | Return `dict[dataset_name, dict[task_id, ...]]` of all datasets |
{% endif %}| `retrieve_task()` | Return sandbox source, problem statement, and resource requirements |
| `setup_task()` | Prepare the sandbox before evaluation (upload files, run install commands) |
| `evaluate_response()` | Score a plain-text response without a sandbox |
| `evaluate_instance()` | Run tests / evaluation scripts in the sandbox |
| `calculate_final_score()` | Aggregate per-task results into a single score |

`setup_task` and `evaluate_instance` are async generators — yield `StreamMessageChunk`, `StreamErrorChunk`, and finally `StreamResultChunk`.

## Authentication

{% if template == "vals-ai" %}
`ExampleBenchmark` extends `DatasetBenchmarkService`; `main.py` uses `DatasetBenchmarkServiceApp`. These shared classes already include Vals authentication and `/v1/*` routes. No additional parent classes or copied authentication files are needed.

Set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true` to enable Descope authentication, catalog/allowlist access, quotas, and trial restrictions. Configure `DESCOPE_PROJECT_ID` and access through `BENCHMARK_CATALOG_API_URL` plus `SERVICE_NAME`, `DESCOPE_TENANT_ALLOWLIST_JSON`, or `DESCOPE_ALLOWLIST_PATH`. Requests then require a Descope access key in `X-Descope-Api-Key`. Quota-enabled services also require `SERVICE_NAME` and `EVALUATION_QUOTA_TABLE_NAME`.

Framework upgrades also update the shared Vals behavior. Local `/v1/*` requests work without credentials when `AUTH_REQUIRED` is unset or false.
{% else %}
Set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true` to require authentication. Implement `check_auth()` for boolean authentication, or `resolve_tenant()` and `check_dataset_access()` for tenant-aware access. With authentication required, the default rejects requests until you implement these hooks. This app includes the shared HTTP and WebSocket routes; it has no `/v1/*` routes.
{% endif %}

Authentication is disabled by default. Hosted registry deployments set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true`. `AUTH_DISABLED` is no longer supported and cannot override that setting.

